{"title":"NOC Engineer Roadmap","role":"NOC Engineer","summary":"A NOC (Network Operations Center) Engineer monitors, maintains, troubleshoots, and supports an organization's IT and network infrastructure.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Computer Science & Engineering (Networks)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A NOC (Network Operations Center) Engineer monitors, maintains, troubleshoots, and supports an organization's IT and network infrastructure."},{"type":"p","text":"The role focuses on ensuring that networks, servers, connectivity, applications, and infrastructure services remain available, stable, and secure."},{"type":"p","text":"A NOC Engineer typically works with monitoring systems, routers, switches, firewalls, VPNs, servers, cloud infrastructure, alerts, incidents, and service-level agreements."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical Responsibilities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Monitor network and infrastructure systems"},{"text":"Investigate alerts and incidents"},{"text":"Troubleshoot connectivity problems"},{"text":"Monitor routers, switches and firewalls"},{"text":"Analyze network performance"},{"text":"Manage incidents and escalations"},{"text":"Perform network configuration changes"},{"text":"Monitor servers and cloud infrastructure"},{"text":"Maintain operational documentation"},{"text":"Track uptime and SLA compliance"},{"text":"Perform root-cause analysis"},{"text":"Coordinate with network, security and infrastructure teams"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Direction","Example Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"Network Operations"},{"text":"NOC Engineer, Network Operations Engineer"}],[{"text":"Network Engineering"},{"text":"Network Engineer"}],[{"text":"Infrastructure"},{"text":"Infrastructure Engineer"}],[{"text":"Cloud"},{"text":"Cloud Network Engineer"}],[{"text":"Network Security"},{"text":"Network Security Engineer"}],[{"text":"Systems"},{"text":"Systems Engineer"}],[{"text":"DevOps"},{"text":"DevOps Engineer"}],[{"text":"Site Reliability"},{"text":"SRE"}],[{"text":"Network Automation"},{"text":"Network Automation Engineer"}],[{"text":"Architecture"},{"text":"Network Architect"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"A NOC role can therefore be an excellent entry point into network engineering, cloud infrastructure, cybersecurity, DevOps, or SRE."}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Networking & Computing Foundation","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build the fundamental technical base."},{"type":"h","text":"Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"C/C++"},{"text":"Data structures"},{"text":"Basic algorithms"},{"text":"Bash scripting"},{"text":"Git/GitHub"},{"text":"Python becomes particularly useful later for network automation."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Computer Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Computer organization"},{"text":"Operating systems"},{"text":"Linux fundamentals"},{"text":"Virtualization"},{"text":"Storage"},{"text":"File systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Networking Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"OSI model"},{"text":"TCP/IP model"},{"text":"Ethernet"},{"text":"MAC addresses"},{"text":"IP addressing"},{"text":"IPv4"},{"text":"IPv6"},{"text":"Subnetting"},{"text":"ARP"},{"text":"ICMP"},{"text":"DNS"},{"text":"DHCP"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year-1 Target"},{"type":"p","text":"Be able to explain how a packet travels from:"},{"type":"flow","items":["User device","Switch","Router","ISP","Internet","Server"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Core Network Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop strong networking skills."},{"type":"h","text":"Routing & Switching"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"VLANs"},{"text":"Trunking"},{"text":"STP"},{"text":"Routing tables"},{"text":"Static routin